{
  "summary": "The `tcp_chat` repository implements a command-line chat system using a custom line protocol defined in `protocol.py` for handling commands and length-prefixed frames. The system relies on a threaded TCP chat server managed by `server.py`, which handles one thread per connected client, enforces unique nicknames, and manages message broadcasting. Users connect to this server via the command-line interface provided in `client.py`. Additionally, the repository includes a test suite that uses pytest to verify the project's functionality."
}
